============================================================================================
LOW-HEIGHT RELATION MOTIFS
============================================================================================
Each vector n below is tested against S_a.  The defect is sum_i S_a[i]*n_i = c*a+d.  A zero defect is an exact relation; the listed z is one oriented reciprocal term.

                 motif                         n       defect height    a exact    term z when exact
 universal_h2_positive     (1, 1, -1, -1, -2, 2) +0a+0      2 [2, 3, 4, 5, 6]     +7.403726469e-05
        a2_h2_negative    (-1, 2, -1, -1, -2, 2) +1a-2      2        [2]     -3.135619413e-05
        a4_h3_negative    (-1, 3, -1, -1, 2, -1) +2a-8      3        [4]     -7.233053203e-05
        a4_h4_negative    (-4, 4, -1, 3, -1, -1) +7a-28      4        [4]     -3.655305842e-05

Readout: the universal height-2 positive relation is shared by every S_a.  The a=4 lift alone has the larger negative height-3/4 resonances shown here, which nearly cancel the positive reservoir before the later shells turn it negative.

